# Generated / local-only
.env
secrets/mcp.signing-key
secrets/mcp.token
# Captures stay untracked HERE and that is deliberate, not an oversight. LIVE4
# in docs/design/backlog.md gives every capture one of three homes, decided
# when it is taken: a committed fixture under tests/pcap-samples/, the private
# corpus reached through SIPNAB_CORPUS, or deletion -- and deletion is the
# default. A capture that sits undecided in a tracked directory is one
# `git add -A` away from being the wrong answer permanently.
#
# Promotion is a deliberate act with a record attached:
#   harness/scripts/capture.sh --name <slug> --pins "<what it pins>"
#   harness/scripts/promote.sh --name <slug>
# The first refuses to run without --pins, because deciding what a capture is
# FOR is cheap while the stack is up and impossible a fortnight later. Five
# undocumented captures sat here for two weeks and had to be deleted rather
# than promoted, for exactly that reason.
captures/*.pcap
captures/*.pcapng
captures/*.json
*.log

# Every credential in this directory, by pattern rather than by name. The list
# used to name `mcp.token` exactly, and the moment a second node needed
# `mcp.token.proxy` and `mcp.token.relay` those were untracked live secrets one
# `git add -A` away from being published. A pattern covers the file nobody has
# thought of yet.
secrets/*.key
secrets/*.token
secrets/*.token.*
secrets/mcp.signing-key*

# Run artefacts: timestamped output of a local end-to-end run, not source.
results/

# Generated media fixtures. `make-pcma-pcap.py` produces these deterministically
# and the setup docs tell you to run it, so committing the output would put a
# megabyte of binary in the tree that can drift from the generator that claims
# to produce it. The stock g711a.pcap/g722.pcap are third-party captures and
# stay tracked.
sipp/scenarios/g711a_answer.pcap
sipp/scenarios/g711a_caller.pcap
